Made improvement of these aspects:
-Logging management;
-Exception handling;
-Driver configuration management

## 🚀 이슈 번호

**Resolve:** {#608}

## 🧩 문제 해결

**시간 내 해결:** ✅ 26M 02S

### 🔎 접근 과정

> 문제 해결을 위한 접근 방식을 설명해주세요.

- 🔹 **어떤 알고리즘을 사용했는지** 정렬, 그리디, 브루트포스
- 🔹 **어떤 방식으로 접근했는지** 큰 순서대로 정렬한 후에 1씩 빼줬습니다. 매 반복마다 정렬을 해야하는데 못해서 중간에 틀렸습니다.

### ⏱️ 시간 복잡도

> **시간 복잡도 분석을 작성해주세요.**  
> 최악의 경우 수행 시간은 어느 정도인지 분석합니다.

- **Big-O 표기법:** `O(N^2logN)`
- **이유:** 정렬이 들어갔기 때문에

## 💻 구현 코드

```python
#include <iostream>
#include <algorithm>
using namespace std;

int n;
int total=0;
int cnt=0;
int arr[101];
void input(){
	cin>>n;

	for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
		cin>>arr[i];
		total+=arr[i];
	}
	sort(arr,arr+100,greater<int> ());
}

void solve(){
	while(cnt<=1440){

		if(total==0){
			cout<<cnt;
			return;
		}
		sort(arr,arr+100,greater<int> ());
	
		for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
			if(!arr[i]) continue;
			cnt++;
			total--;
			arr[i]--;
			for(int j=i+1;j<n;j++){
				if(!arr[j]) continue;
				total--;
				arr[j]--;
				// cout<<i<<" "<<j<<" "<<cnt<<" "<<total<<"\n";
				break;
			}
			break;
		}
	}
	cout<<"-1";
}

int main(){
	input();
	solve();
}
```

This PR finalises my efforts over the past few days to complete the first version of Logic Rondo. From this point onward, no new features will be added to this version of the tool. It will still be maintained while it is in use. Development will start at a later point on a second edition that uses tree-based verification, requiring significant modification to how verification is performed.

More specifically, this PR contains the following:
- Closes #1, variable assumption is now a proper rule;
- Closes #13, proof checking with regard to a signature is now supported;
- Further improves #14, ensuring ALL range references are checked to be to begin and end;
- Closes #17, the test has been modified to pass;
- Closes #18, proof checking with regard to restricting to prop. logic is now supported;
- Closes #23, manual position configuration is now implemented. The selected option persists between different site visits;
- Closes #26 through implementing a small state machine;
- Closes #33 by checking whitespace.
- Closes #35.

This allows configurations to potentially specify a more minimal set of information


Normally you would have to specify all the info for an adapter e.g. like this

```json
{
  "type": "BedGraphTabixAdapter",
  "bedGraphGzLocation": {
    "uri": "https://jbrowse.org/genomes/GRCh38/1000g/kidd_lab_cnv/PUR/HG01414.qm2.CN.1k.simp.bed.gz"
  },
  "index": {
    "location": {
      "uri": "https://jbrowse.org/genomes/GRCh38/1000g/kidd_lab_cnv/PUR/HG01414.qm2.CN.1k.simp.bed.gz.tbi"
    }
  }
}
```


With this PR, a user can pass


```json
{
  "type": "BedGraphTabixAdapter",
  "uri": "file.bed.gz"
}
```


and it would infer that this is "bedGraphGzLocation":{"uri":"file.bed.gz"}


one possible downside is this can create a conflict between ingested config and exported config. for example, round tripping this through admin-server, would result in any of the 'simple' forms being removed most likely, unless bookkeeping was done about the simple form to also postProcessSnapshot

however, the upsides i think are significant: simple config is important
